    },
    "message": "Surface LLM rule fallbacks in Run summaries\n\nAPI-mode runs could silently fall back to rules for every task (call cap,\ndenied usage allowance, schema rejection) while the manifest reported\nfailures: 0, so results matching offline looked like a model problem.\n\n- Add sheltersim.llm.outcomes: one classifier that counts accepted,\n  fallback and offline-rule calls by reason, error kind and prompt version\n  and derives a status (not_requested / offline_rules / all_accepted /\n  degraded / all_fallback).\n- Manifest llm_usage gains a versioned \"outcomes\" block; \"failures\" now\n  counts every non-offline fallback, including max_api_calls and\n  shared_allowance_unavailable.\n- CLI run prints llm_status and warns on stderr when degraded or\n  all_fallback (exit code unchanged).\n- Add read-only Project route .../branches/{branch}/llm-status computed\n  from records already in the head Checkpoint (no Checkpoint format change).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
